# Security response headers for every path Netlify serves (#122). Netlify reads this file from
# the publish directory on every deploy, CLI deploys included; the build copies it there from
# public/, like _redirects. The ADR is docs/DECISIONS.md, 2026-10-01.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy, directive by directive:
#
#   script-src 'self'       Nothing but this origin's own files. No inline script and no eval:
#                           the app loads no third-party script, and Angular's AOT output needs
#                           neither. This is the line that turns an injected <script> or event
#                           handler into a console error. It is also why angular.json turns off
#                           critical-CSS inlining: that emits <link onload="this.media='all'">,
#                           an inline handler this directive blocks, which would leave the full
#                           stylesheet stuck at media="print" (security-headers.spec.ts).
#   style-src 'unsafe-inline'  Required, not a shortcut. Angular injects every component's
#                           styles as <style> elements at runtime, and the nonce that would avoid
#                           this has to be fresh per response, which a static host cannot do.
#                           Injected CSS can restyle the page; it cannot run script.
#   img-src https:          Project images are external URLs an admin pastes in
#                           (docs/DATA_MODEL.md). An allowlist of hosts would break the next
#                           image from a new host silently: the card would fall back to its
#                           generated artwork and look intentional. http: is not listed;
#                           browsers upgrade an http image on an https page before this applies.
#   connect-src             This origin, plus the API's. KEEP IT IN STEP with apiBaseUrl in
#                           src/environments/environment.ts: a stale origin here blocks every
#                           API call. api-origin-hints.spec.ts fails if apiBaseUrl's origin is
#                           missing from this line.
#   frame-ancestors 'none'  Nothing may frame this site, the admin pages included: clickjacking.
#                           X-Frame-Options: DENY says the same to browsers that predate CSP2.
#
# default-src 'self' covers everything not named (frames, workers, media, manifests).
# object-src and base-uri are named because default-src does not cover base-uri, and object-src
# 'none' is cheaper to state than to reason about.

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' https:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://tarka1939.bieda.it; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
